ter Crosby, who has raised roughly $60,000 and reports minimal money on hand. Prediction markets give Moore roughly a 95 percent chance of holding the seat.\n\nThe only public survey, commissioned by Crosby's own campaign, showed a 32-to-31 contest with a large undecided share, and a statewide network of anti-Trump activists has endorsed the Democrat. Given the district's partisan lean and the fundraising gap, that poll likely reflects low challenger name recognition more than a genuine toss-up. A Libertarian and two independents are also on the ballot, but none is viewed as a significant factor.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0478, "margin": -11.61}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0598, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0822, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0672, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0948, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0534, "margin": -12.0}]}